      ],
      "skos:notation": "ITU",
      "skos:scopeNote": "Singular 'Telecommunication' (the official UN agency name) in SC abbreviations (who-iris/library/9789240101197-eng/sections/page-007.md, p. 7), PC (who-iris/library/9789240116191-eng/sections/page-013.md, \"ITU = International Telecommunication Union\"), and RA front matter (library/who-dpi-h-reference-architecture-draft-v1/sections/sec-front-matter.md). Wording variant in PHC abbreviations (who-iris/library/9789240093362-eng/sections/sec-001-abbreviations.md, pp. 7-8): \"International Telecommunications Union\" (plural). Recorded per smart-ra#133 S1 and smart-ra#200.",
      "dcterms:source": "who-iris/library/9789240101197-eng/sections/page-007.md",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/smart-ra/v0/ns/glossary/dpi-h-ra/non-functional-requirements",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/smart-ra/v0/ns/glossary/dpi-h-ra"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "Non-Functional Requirements"
        }
      ],
      "skos:altLabel": [
        "Non-functional requirements",
        "nonfunctional requirements"
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "General attributes and features of the digital system to ensure usability and overcome technical and physical constraints. Examples of non-functional requirements include ability to work offline, multiple language settings, and password protection (see section 3.8)."
        }
      ],
      "skos:scopeNote": "PHC handbook glossary wording, verbatim (who-iris/library/9789240093362-eng/sections/sec-002-glossary.md, p. 10), identical (without section cross-reference) in SFP handbook glossary (who-iris/library/9789240120747-eng/sections/page-010.md, p. 10). Substantive alternatives across the DTH corpus (smart-ra#133 S1): (1) SC handbook glossary ('nonfunctional requirements', who-iris/library/9789240101197-eng/sections/page-008.md, p. 8): \"A description of how the digital system needs to operate and perform in order to support the tasks that make up the business process.\" (2) PC handbook glossary ('Non-functional requirements', who-iris/library/9789240116191-eng/sections/page-008.md, p. 8): \"Description of the attributes and constraints that the system must have to ensure its quality and performance. These requirements do not specify what the system should do, but rather how the system should perform its functions. (e.g., a product master data management solution must be able to support offline mode when network connectivity is not available)\" All are recorded as candidates; none is chosen.",
      "skos:related": [
        {
          "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/smart-ra/v0/ns/glossary/dpi-h-ra/functional-requirements"
        }
      ],
      "dcterms:source": "who-iris/library/9789240093362-eng/sections/sec-002-glossary.md",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/smart-ra/v0/ns/glossary/dpi-h-ra/open-architectures",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/smart-ra/v0/ns/glossary/dpi-h-ra"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "Open Architectures"
        }
      ],
      "skos:altLabel": [
        "open architectures"
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "Open architectures refer to high-level specifications of technical designs that provide blueprints for creating open ecosystems structured into reusable and shareable components."
        }
      ],
      "skos:scopeNote": "RA §2.2.2 body wording, verbatim (library/who-dpi-h-reference-architecture-draft-v1/sections/sec-022-222-the-enabling-conditions-for-reddhi.md, p. 35–39), citing Mehl et al. 2023 (library/mehl-2023-full-stac-oqad018/, glossary/full-stac.glossary.json: \"High-level specifications of technical designs that provide blueprints for creating open ecosystems structured into reusable and shareable components, such as within a health information exchange.\"). Linked via exactMatch to the full-STAC scheme (smart-ra#133 S1, smart-ra#143).",
      "skos:related": [
